cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TeX Authorship, we appreciate if you cite it.:)"
type: software
title: "TeX Authorship: authorship tracking for LaTeX in VS Code"
abstract: >-
  A VS Code extension and LuaLaTeX package that mark passages of a LaTeX
  document which was written by a co-author, an AI assistant or taken from a reference.
  The syntax is a simple pair of comment lines around each passage.
  This way it travels with the source through formatters, undo and git.
  Marked passages are tinted in the editor and coloured in a draft PDF.
  Developed with AI coding assistance (Claude). 
  The commit history records which changes were made with it.
authors:
  - family-names: "Fürtön"
    given-names: "Balázs"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0073-6208"
license: MIT
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23607060"
repository-code: "https://github.com/odv-hu/tex-authorship"
keywords:
  - LaTeX
  - authorship
  - provenance
  - generative AI
  - disclosure
  - VS Code
